# corpus-hygiene census OUTPUTS are run artifacts, not sources.
# The tools are tracked; their JSON is not. An unstamped census JSON
# sitting in scripts/ reads as current to the next reader.
scripts/*_census.json

# closure_run.py is a DISPOSABLE runner, not an instrument. It exists because
# check_T_ie_full_surface_input_inventory and check_RT_dag_chain need a native
# single-process run that no sandbox can reach. Canonical copy lives in
# __APF Library/Artifacts_2026-08-09_session/closure_run/. Ignored here so a
# `git add -A` cannot sweep a throwaway runner or its transcripts into a commit.
# RULED 2026-08-09: disposable, NOT a kept tool -- making it one re-opens the
# corpus-hygiene instrument freeze, and nothing about it needs to be pinned.
closure_run.py
closure_run_*.log
